 Part A — Audit of the Stage 6.8 "oracle" anomaly

**The anomaly.** In Stage 6.8, the arm with full information about the exact
causal influence of every candidate actuator did *worse* than the arm that had
to estimate that influence by finite probing. A full-information method losing
to its own noisy estimate is a signal that the information was being used for
the wrong quantity, so it was audited before any new experiment was run.

Reproduction: 8 episodes × 6 arms at the Stage 6.8 operating point, 12 logged
quantities per timestep per arm (`data/audit_trace.json`), then six hypotheses
tested separately with common random numbers (`data/audit_hypotheses.json`).

